From 8867ecdc6f26c22424c46e22ffc6df36fb499d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:32:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(raw): only refuse a write overlapping a mounted partition

Writing a bootloader to the gap ahead of the first partition of a disk was
refused whenever any partition of that disk was mounted, as is always the
case for the running rootfs:

  target device "/dev/mmcblk1" is in use, it holds the filesystem mounted
  at "/"

The raw handler now checks only the region it writes, so partitions of a
whole disk lying outside of it are ignored. The disk itself, its holders,
overlapping partitions and partitions with unreadable bounds are still
checked, as is any other target. raw-delta keeps the exclusive check, as
its written length is not known up front.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/UpdateHub/updatehub/pull/460]

Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 updatehub/src/object/installer/raw.rs | 70 ++++++++++++++------
 updatehub/src/utils/definitions.rs    | 13 +++-
 updatehub/src/utils/fs.rs             | 93 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 153 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

